// TEST: an explicit width cast of a literal still converts it
// ============================================================================
// R19 refuses a literal that does not fit the width its CONTEXT gives it; an
// explicit cast is a conversion, not an adaptation (formalism 2.4), and keeps
// master's behaviour: Int32 wraps, Float32 overflows to an infinity (f prints inf) -- as the
// same casts of a run-time value. (An open item for the user: whether a cast
// of a constant that cannot fit should be refused too.)
// ============================================================================
let w = Int32(5000000000)
let f = Float32(1e40)
let f_overflowed = f > 3.0e38
// EXPECT: w = 705032704
// EXPECT: f_overflowed = true
